# Sensorimotor Alignment — machine-local path configuration TEMPLATE
#
# COPY this file to `paths.env` and EDIT every value marked `# EDIT:` below.
# `paths.env` is gitignored so your local edits stay out of commits.
#
# How it is loaded:
#   - From shell:      `set -a && source paths.env && set +a`
#   - From Python:     `import config` (reads paths.env automatically)
#
# Code repos are vendored under `repos/` inside this project — there is
# nothing to clone or symlink. The only things you must point at are
# external resources: the conda root, raw datasets, and large checkpoints.

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 1. Workspace root and conda
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Where YOU keep this project. EDIT if not at $HOME/vla.
WORK="${WORK:-$HOME/vla}"

# Conda root — auto-detected from `which conda` if you have conda on PATH.
# Override only if your envs live somewhere else.
CONDA_ROOT="${CONDA_ROOT:-$(dirname "$(dirname "$(command -v conda 2>/dev/null)")" 2>/dev/null)}"
CONDA_ROOT="${CONDA_ROOT:-$HOME/miniconda3}"      # fallback if conda not on PATH

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 2. Raw datasets — REQUIRED for Tier 3 (rebuild Stage-A subsets from RLDS)
#    See README §"Dataset setup" for download commands.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# DROID v1.0.1 RLDS (single-arm Franka, ~1.7 TB raw)
#   Public source: gs://gresearch/robotics/droid/1.0.1
# EDIT: point at your DROID download
BRIDGE_RLDS_DIR="${BRIDGE_RLDS_DIR:-${WORK}/datasets/openvla/bridge_orig/1.0.0}"
DROID_RLDS_DIR="${DROID_RLDS_DIR:-${WORK}/datasets/droid/1.0.1}"

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 3. Model checkpoints — needed only to re-run Stage B (feature extraction)
#    All others auto-download from HuggingFace (set HF_HOME below).
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# SimplerEnv-OpenVLA harness root (for RT-1-X / Octo / OpenVLA-7B reference ckpts)
SIMPLER_ROOT="${SIMPLER_ROOT:-${WORK}/SimplerEnv-OpenVLA}"
CKPT_OPENVLA_7B="${CKPT_OPENVLA_7B:-${SIMPLER_ROOT}/checkpoints/openvla-7b}"
CKPT_OPENVLA_FT="${CKPT_OPENVLA_FT:-${SIMPLER_ROOT}/checkpoints/openvla-bridge-sft}"
CKPT_RT1X="${CKPT_RT1X:-${SIMPLER_ROOT}/rt_1_x_tf_trained_for_002272480_step}"

# GR00T checkpoints (download from HuggingFace under nvidia/GR00T-...)
CKPT_GROOT_N15="${CKPT_GROOT_N15:-${WORK}/checkpoints/GR00T-N1.5-Lerobot-SimplerEnv-BridgeV2}"
CKPT_GROOT_N16="${CKPT_GROOT_N16:-${WORK}/checkpoints/GR00T-N1.6-bridge}"

# Raw Prismatic (gated on HF Hub; optional — not used by paper experiments)
CKPT_PRISMATIC_RAW="${CKPT_PRISMATIC_RAW:-${WORK}/prismatic-vlms-hf/prism-dinosiglip-224px+7b}"

# StarVLA pretrained models directory (5 finetuned VLAs, ~80 GB)
# README §VLA-SR's feature-extraction loop downloads each StarVLA bundle
# directly via `huggingface-cli download` and does not consult this variable,
# but tests/test_paths.py still checks that the dir exists.
CKPT_STARVLA_DIR="${CKPT_STARVLA_DIR:-${WORK}/starVLA/playground/Pretrained_models}"

# Per-experiment checkpoints (WAM-SR §3.3, freeze-ablation §4.2) are intentionally
# NOT defined here — each Reproducing section in README.md owns its own download
# commands so you only fetch the checkpoints for the experiments you actually run.
# See README.md §"Reproducing WAM-SR / 2. Feature extraction" and §"Reproducing
# Additional Findings (§4) / §4.2 Freeze-vs-unfreeze ablation" for the full lists.

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 4. DATA_STORE — where Stage A/B/C caches live
#    ~30 GB committed CSVs + ~600 GB peak during Tier-3 from-scratch
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# EDIT: pick a fast disk with plenty of room
DATA_STORE="${DATA_STORE:-${WORK}/cknna_data_store}"
RECORD_DIR="${RECORD_DIR:-${DATA_STORE}/record}"

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 5. HuggingFace cache — many extractors auto-download
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Set HF_HOME to keep model downloads on a big disk
HF_HOME="${HF_HOME:-${WORK}/hf_cache}"

# If any model is gated (CogACT needs meta-llama/Llama-2-7b-hf),
# either run `huggingface-cli login` or export HF_TOKEN here:
# HF_TOKEN="hf_..."

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 6. Model-metadata CSV (paper figure key → benchmark mapping)
#    Resolved from repo root by default; override only to use a custom file.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# META_CSV="${WORK}/cknna_project/data/performance/model_metadata.csv"
